- name: 
- description: The Experiment Velocity Band metric quantifies the speed and throughput of machine learning experimentation by tracking the number of experiment iterations, or runs, completed within a week, as well as the time taken to complete each run. This metric provides insights into the efficiency of the experimentation process, helping teams identify potential bottlenecks that may hinder rapid iteration and innovation. It encompasses all stages of the experimentation lifecycle, from initial setup and data preparation to model training and evaluation. By monitoring this metric, organizations can assess the effectiveness of their training pipelines and make informed decisions to optimize resource allocation. Additionally, it serves as a key indicator for the overall health of the ML workflow, influencing deployment strategies and continuous integration/continuous deployment (CI/CD) practices.

