Metric:
- id: mlflow.registry_hygiene_band
- name: 
- description: The Model Registry Hygiene Band metric evaluates the organization and clarity of the model registry within an ML lifecycle. It assesses adherence to naming conventions, appropriate usage of model stages (such as development, staging, and production), and the implementation of deprecation practices for outdated models. This metric aims to identify cluttered or ambiguous states in the registry that can lead to confusion among data scientists and engineers. By monitoring these aspects, teams can ensure that the model registry remains a reliable source of truth for model management. A well-maintained registry facilitates smoother ML experimentation, training, and deployment processes, ultimately enhancing the overall efficiency of the MLOps pipeline.

