- description: The Endpoint Service Level Objective Band metric measures the adherence of deployed machine learning endpoints to predefined Service Level Agreements (SLAs) concerning latency, uptime, and error budgets. It evaluates whether the endpoints are meeting the expected performance criteria, which are critical for ensuring reliable and efficient model serving in production environments. This metric flags any violations of the SLAs, indicating potential issues that could affect user experience or system reliability. Additionally, it identifies unstable serving deployments that may not consistently meet performance expectations, allowing teams to take corrective actions. By monitoring this metric, organizations can ensure that their machine learning models are not only operational but also performing within acceptable limits, thereby maintaining trust in automated decision-making systems.

