- description: The Production Monitoring Coverage metric assesses the extent to which monitoring practices are implemented for machine learning models in production. It evaluates key components such as drift detection, performance dashboards, and alerting rules, which are essential for maintaining model integrity and performance over time. This metric identifies potential blind spots in the oversight of live models, ensuring that all critical aspects of model behavior are being tracked. By measuring the coverage of these monitoring activities, organizations can gain insights into the robustness of their model governance and the effectiveness of their response mechanisms. A comprehensive monitoring strategy is vital for early detection of issues that could impact model performance and business outcomes.

