- description: The Cost Correlation Band metric measures the relationship between the computational resources utilized during machine learning (ML) workloads and the resulting outputs or performance metrics of those workloads. It aims to identify inefficiencies in spending by analyzing how variations in compute usage correlate with the effectiveness of model training and experimentation outcomes. This metric encompasses various stages of the ML lifecycle, including experimentation, training pipelines, and deployment. By flagging instances where high compute usage does not correspond to improved model performance, it helps teams optimize resource allocation and reduce unnecessary costs. The scope of this metric includes all aspects of ML operations, from initial experimentation through to model serving and monitoring, ensuring a comprehensive view of cost efficiency across the entire ML workflow.

