Metric:
- id: sm.endpoint_slo_scaling_band
- name: 
- description: This metric measures the adherence of service level objectives (SLOs) for machine learning model endpoints during scaling events, specifically focusing on autoscaling latency and throughput. It captures the system's ability to maintain performance standards when demand fluctuates, indicating how well the infrastructure can adapt to increased load. The metric flags instances of overload, where the system fails to meet SLOs due to insufficient resources, as well as slow ramp-up behavior, where the system takes longer than expected to scale up to meet demand. By monitoring this metric, teams can identify potential bottlenecks in the deployment and serving phases of the ML lifecycle. It is crucial for ensuring that models remain responsive and reliable under varying traffic conditions, thereby supporting effective ML experimentation and operational stability.

