Metric:
- id: sm.cost_efficiency_band
- name: 
- description: This metric evaluates the efficiency of Amazon SageMaker workloads by analyzing instance utilization, idle compute resources, and the relationship between training costs and output quality. It measures how effectively computational resources are being used during machine learning experimentation and training pipelines, indicating whether resources are being over-provisioned or under-utilized. The metric also considers the cost incurred relative to the performance of the trained models, providing insights into the trade-offs between resource expenditure and model accuracy or other quality metrics. By monitoring this metric, organizations can identify opportunities for optimizing their ML workflows, ensuring that they achieve the best possible outcomes while minimizing unnecessary costs. The scope of this metric encompasses all stages of the ML lifecycle, from experimentation through deployment and serving, making it a critical component of effective MLOps practices.

