- description: This metric quantifies the frequency at which machine learning models and related services are deployed into production environments. It encompasses all deployment activities, including updates to existing models, the introduction of new models, and changes to associated services that support model inference. A higher deployment frequency typically indicates a mature MLOps practice, reflecting an organization's ability to iterate quickly and respond to changing business needs or model performance issues. The metric is bounded by the deployment activities that are part of the continuous integration and continuous deployment (CI/CD) pipeline, ensuring that only relevant deployments are counted. It serves as an indicator of the efficiency and effectiveness of the ML experimentation and training pipelines, as well as the overall health of the model registry and serving infrastructure.

