Metric:
- id: cicd.lead_time_band
- name: 
- description: This metric measures the duration from the moment a code commit is made in the version control system until the corresponding machine learning service is successfully deployed and operational. It encompasses the entire CI/CD pipeline, including stages such as automated testing, model training, and any manual approval processes that may be in place. By evaluating this lead time, organizations can identify inefficiencies in their ML experimentation and deployment workflows, such as prolonged training pipelines or delays caused by manual interventions. The metric serves as an indicator of the agility and responsiveness of the ML development process, highlighting areas that may require optimization to enhance deployment speed. It is crucial for ensuring that models can be iteratively improved and delivered to production in a timely manner, thereby supporting continuous integration and delivery practices in machine learning operations.

